wildos-backup (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Drives plugged in lists every drive you plug in. One Backup can't use
    is greyed and says why: a Wild OS installer stick, a disc image,
    read-only, too small, a filesystem Backup can't write to, or locked.
    Format this drive is offered where formatting would fix it.
  * Backup no longer waits for a drive when the one plugged in can't be
    used: it says no drive here can hold backups yet.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:49:40 +0000

